  "notes": "Authored for due2; no origin result. Shows several policies per case at work: the case has two policy files, policy.ttl and policy-embargo.ttl, which are one corpus (conformance/README.md). Within ex:licence, conflict perm lets ex:readLicensed eliminate ex:noInternal; across the policies, any surviving T prohibition eliminates every candidate (prohibit-overrides). Scenario 1 shows that a prohibition eliminated within its own policy does not override across policies, and scenario 3 that both rules apply in one evaluation. A reader that applies one policy's conflict strategy to the whole corpus gets scenario 1 or 2 wrong, whichever policy it picks.",
